  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through Wednesday)\nIssued at 1225 AM CST Thu Nov 12 2026\n\nFriday night the upper ridge will get pushed to the east as another \ntrough digs across the southwest. The old frontal boundary will \nstill be in the vicinity. The combination of the upper trough and \nsurface boundary will bring chances for rain for the weekend. Rain \nchances will spread across from west to east beginning after \nmidnight Friday night out west spreading over the entire area \nSaturday and moving off to the east Sunday. Models have continued to \nshow only moderate rainfall totals with no significant impacts. An \nupper level ridge will move in starting Monday bringing dry weather \nback for the first few days of next week. \n\nWith cloudy skies and showers, temperatures will be cooler over the \nweekend. After the rain moves away Monday winds will become \nnortheasterly bringing in cooler, drier air. Temperatures Monday and \nTuesday will be as much as 10 degrees cooler than the weekend. \nWednesday there will start a warming trend.",
